ly be safe is to be  very honest that way you're never caught  fame you know a lot of people use famous  propaganda to make themselves seem more  perfect  more talented more beautiful than they  are and it's not the truth and you  always get found out  so for me the way to take the pressure  off was to be very honest about myself  and my fans really embraced that and  you know being a singer-songwriter is  different than being  a singer or a pop star  or even a rock you know star like being  a singer songwriter means you have to  care about people you have to care about  honesty  you know there can only be about three  or four songs about love and the rest  better better be about society and what  we're seeing around us  and it really is this sacred uh  thing you know that bob dylan and neil  young really instilled in me  when i toured with them of what that  means and your relationship with people  um and it's been an incredible  relationship my fan base ended up  calling themselves the everyday angels  from a line in a song of mine called i'm  sensitive and it's just about the fact  that when we're honest with each other  and we help each other we have the power  to work basically miracles and we forget  how much power as individuals we have  and i mean that's an amazing thing to  have a fan base rally around  you know these songs became more than  just like  singles they became part of the  landscape it  comes it almost feels like you just know  them  they just kind of lived in you if you  were you know alive at that time  listening to them how was your  relationship with this music  changed over time and how are you like  what keeps you excited about these songs  now 25 years later  i'm going to do a live stream show on  october  no sorry november 20th and  i'm learning all the songs i'm going to  sing the whole album in sequence i've  never done it before i've never sung all  these songs in one  place like this and so i'm going back  and learning  a lot of these strange open tunings and  these eight minute long songs  and it's like visiting you know friends  uh  and seeing myself now as an artist and  what my art was like  then you know i didn't have any  self-awareness honestly at that time  of what my art was like um and it's neat  it's neat to see  you know my 16 year old self like really  struggling to find a way to express  emotions and  i'm really excited for the show because  singing them in order is really  it's powerful to me like it definitely  makes me cry it's a very  much more cathartic thing than i thought  it would be as well what's standing out  to you about the songs now as you're  relearning them  revisiting them  uh i think what stands out is i can i  can hear what i was reading you know in  alaska i grew up without electricity we  didn't listen to  to music but i read a lot and so a lot  of the russian  writers that were very like  revolutionary you know writing for the  common man this very like  passionate writing and same with a lot  of latin american  poets that i was reading at the time um  i can hear a lot of leonard cohen you  know so i can really hear my  influences and that i didn't have any  rules you know i was writing eight  minute long songs that were like folk  operas  because i didn't know songs had to have  a structure and there's a lot of uh  creative freedom when you don't know the  rules and it definitely made me want to  go back to saying okay i gotta forget  some of the rules  nice are you excited to be able to reach  out to people  the way that you're going to on the 20th  in this livestream is much different  than  you know performing for an audience a  live audience  i'm really excited about the the live  show um there's a beautiful theater in  the town where i live so i'm going to go  in there it's an old theater from the  1900s and we have three cameras and i  wanted it to be like a really beautiful  shoot not like a zoom  concert uh and i'm excited because i  have a lot of fans all over the world  i've never really gotten to see i've  never been to south america  there's lots of countries that i quit  touring a long time ago and so  because it's this pandemic and because  we have to do things virtually i can  actually do something where  australia and everybody can tune in  which i'm very excited about  when we're allowed to travel again would  you reconsider would you  think about going on tour again yeah  yeah i don't know if i'll tour you know  this anniversary i have a new record  coming out  and uh i'd probably tour that um but  we'll see how much i like doing this  you know the sequence of songs from that  first album we'll see  and you've also been very uh vocal about  using your platform promoting  conversations about mental health  including anxiety depression isolation  why why has that been such an important  thing for you  you know we're all we all have this  brain inside this box  and we all have pain but none of us are  taught what to do with pain in school  it's kind of bizarre that realized  everything i was taught in school  didn't actually help me be a happy  person and what's the point what's the  point of being good at math or having a  good job if you're not  happy if you don't know how to handle  stress and anxiety  i think we've lost a lot of those skill  sets and that's what i was most  interested in  because my number one job was to figure  out how to be happy and so i spent a  lifetime accumulating knowledge to help  me gain  tone and mental fitness and emotional  fitness and career fitness  as well as physical fitness nutritional  and parenting fitness we have to gain  educations in this otherwise we feel  really unbalanced and it's not  harmonious  so these tools that i learned when i was  homeless to help solve for my anxiety  they're just little tools that i  invented  and they were actually proven to work by  a neuroscientist named dr judson brewer  to really rewire your brain  and so i started just creating a youth  foundation  where we help at-risk youth using those  tools  a public school curriculum where it's an  english class you know regular core  english class every school has the money  for that  but it has these mindfulness tools built  into it and then right now  i'm starting up there's a festival we  have again with this whole human model  of helping people get education  and then also a culture company for  businesses to help create a culture in a  company that helps  solve for pain and their employees and  make them more productive  that's amazing you know with all that  experience and knowledge and work is  there anything you would go back  in time if you could 25 years and tell  yourself  from what you've learned now i would  definitely tell myself that  being hyper vigilant doesn't help you  win  you know it doesn't even keep you safe  it just keeps you very busy  uh what actually kept me safe was just  not quitting  and i mean emotionally um not not really  with my career although not quitting  there helped too but  stubbornness isn't you know a bad  quality when it comes to  learning how to be happy you just have  to keep saying i'm gonna do something  different today and it's that tenacity  that eventually  will get you there so if i could have  learned to relax and just trust that  process and that with time it would  happen  um that probably would have saved me a  lot of stress it seems like you have so  much going on  are you excited for the holidays would  you take a little bit of time to relax  you know i really love the life i built  there's a song called painters on my  first album of a woman that says  you know i'm painting myself a beautiful  world and  i've always taken that really seriously  i want my life to be my best work of art  i don't want my art to be my best art if  my art is my best work of art i'm kind  of an  a-hole i think i want the whole thing to  be  thoughtful and that takes time but  creating a sculpture out of your life  and so i'm not  i'm busy but i'm also a lot of time  quiet i don't tour that often  um i do things i'm passionate about and  it's constantly finding that way to have  permission to say no i get to make this  how i want what do i want it takes a lot  of  introspection but um i'm not tired i  used to be you know i burnt myself out  with my career and it's not like that  anymore um  so i will take time for the holidays but  i'm really happy that i'm being very  productive but not in a way that  exhausts me now and that's a huge change  for me  you

